<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 10 November, from 1202 to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1202</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Fourth Crusade lays siege to the Christian city of Zara</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Crusaders unable to pay the Venetians for their fleet arrived at Zara on the Dalmatian coast and besieged it for Venice. The city fell within two weeks, and Pope Innocent III excommunicated the crusaders.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1775</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Continental Congress creates the Continental Marines</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Continental Congress resolved to raise two battalions of Marines. The date is celebrated as the birthday of the United States Marine Corps.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1871</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry Morton Stanley finds David Livingstone at Ujiji</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The journalist Henry Morton Stanley located the missionary-explorer David Livingstone at Ujiji, on Lake Tanganyika, by Stanley's own dating. His reported greeting, 'Dr Livingstone, I presume?', became famous.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-tanganyika">Lake Tanganyika</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1938</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk dies in Istanbul</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Atatürk, founder and first president of the Republic of Turkey, died at Dolmabahçe Palace. Turks still pause at 9.05 in the morning on this day to mark the moment of his death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal Atatürk</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1975</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The freighter Edmund Fitzgerald sinks in Lake Superior</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The ore carrier SS Edmund Fitzgerald sank in a violent storm on Lake Superior with the loss of all 29 crew. It is the largest ship lost on the Great Lakes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a></div></li></ol>
